      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. They reported search relevance degradation starting from the taxonomy change on 2026-02-20, with saved searches returning low-relevance hits and duplicates, increasing manual triage time to about 6 hours per day [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_bd3560dfe194].\n\nTo get BlueHarbor comfortable with renewal, we proposed a proof plan involving a short-term mitigation that includes updating index weighting and adding a mapping layer to translate new taxonomy terms to historical query tokens for the top 20 saved searches. The plan involves a 7-10 business day A/B test and validation period aiming for a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80%, no regression in suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. If validation passes, a 1-day production rollout and 72-hour monitoring window will follow. This is offered as a 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48,000, with a 30% discount if BlueHarbor concurrently signs an Orchestrator expansion. Additionally, there is a conditional credit clause: if the proof does not meet the agreed metrics within 10 business days, a one-quarter invoice credit prorated against the renewal will be applied [art_bd3560dfe194, art_0bccc580184e].",
