      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant,\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments.\" This inconsistency caused the ingestion normalization to fail to collapse these into a single canonical attribute, leading to Rules Engine matching failures on the entity tag used for routing approvals.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix that involved adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, hot-reloadable, and low risk, allowing immediate remediation without waiting for Okta change control, which would take 2 to 4 weeks [art_79f625aafa16].",
