      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is NordicChem AB. This is based on the executive escalation call and competitor report indicating procurement pressure and consideration of NoiseGuard as a tactical proof of concept, with high retention risk if Northstar misses acceptance milestones [art_25fac9f564e7, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_e89e8accadd2].\n\nThe exact milestone at risk is the remediation plan milestone involving the backfill enrichment and index rebuild scheduled from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30, followed by a validation window from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14. The milestone includes achieving acceptance criteria such as precision@10 >= 0.8 for facility lookups, entity-link hit rate >= 90%, and grouping false-positive rate <= 5%. This milestone is critical to demonstrating measurable noise reduction and restoring search and entity graph correctness [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_25fac9f564e7].\n\nAdditional details include a 30-day retune plan with weekly checkpoints every Friday, and an immediate scoped suppression configuration and correlator window change to be applied by 2026-03-21 02:00 CET to reduce alert noise. A one-time credit of 10% of ACV is offered if milestone acceptance is not met by agreed dates, underscoring the milestone's importance to renewal negotiations [art_25fac9f564e7, art_7373b64fdfdd].\n\nIn summary, NordicChem AB faces high defection risk tied to the milestone of completing the enrichment backfill and index rebuild by end of April 2026, with validation in early May 2026, and failure to meet this milestone may lead procurement to extend NoiseGuard as a cheaper tactical alternative [art_25fac9f564e7, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd].",
