      "answer": "There is a recurring approval-bypass pattern across multiple Canadian accounts after migration from legacy workflow tooling, not just MapleBridge. The affected customers include City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank.\n\nThe shared failure pattern is that after migration, approval workflows for Canada-specific or region-specific policies fail due to incorrect rule evaluation precedence: global-default rules override or bypass country or province-specific overrides. This causes approvals to be stuck, auto-denied, bypassed, or routed incorrectly. This pattern is triggered by migration from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product, where the rules engine evaluates global-default policies with higher or conflicting precedence compared to region-specific overrides. The root cause involves schema normalization issues, delayed schema registry synchronization, or missing merge metadata.\n\nMapleBridge Insurance experienced a one-off timing window issue on 2026-03-12 where a delay in schema registry synchronization caused some rule-evaluation pods to apply global.v3 rules instead of canada.v2 overrides, resulting in about 117 approvals bypassing Canada-specific gating for certain policy types. However, this timing window issue is part of the broader recurring pattern seen across other accounts.\n\nIn plain English, the problem is that after switching to the new Orchestrator system, the system sometimes mistakenly applies general global approval rules before or instead of the specific Canadian regional rules. This causes approvals that should require Canadian-specific checks to be skipped or incorrectly handled, leading to stuck or auto-denied approvals or approvals bypassing required Canadian approvers.\n\nThe customers with this shared failure pattern are:\n- City of Verdant Bay\n- Maple Regional Transit Authority\n- MapleBay Marketplace\n- MapleBridge Insurance\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems\n- MaplePath Career Institute\n- MapleWest Bank\n\nThis is not a MapleBridge-only issue but a recurring problem across these Canadian accounts after migration [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_54e35e2cb431, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_e697b3abe158].",
